   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "f58e2d90",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "Research Question: How does the proportion of fatal motor-vehicle crashes involving alcohol consumption differ between major U.S. holidays and comparable non-holiday periods, and how has this relationship changed from 2019 to 2024?"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 34,
   "id": "76d33680",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import numpy as np\n",
    "import pandas as pd\n",
    "import holidays\n",
    "from datetime import timedelta\n",
    "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "e7e217e4",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "Load and prepare the crash data\n",
    "\n",
    "We first combined the FARS crash-level data from 2019 through 2024. Each row represents one fatal crash. We added the year to each dataset before combining them so that crashes from different years could be identified correctly. "
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 35,
   "id": "ccb51c97",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "YEAR\n",
      "2019    33487\n",
      "2020    35935\n",
      "2021    39785\n",
      "2022    39422\n",
      "2023    37769\n",
      "2024    36297\n",
      "Name: count, dtype: int64\n",
      "Total crashes 222695\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "annual_crashes = []\n",
    "\n",
    "for year in range(2019, 2025):\n",
    "    filename = \"accident.CSV\" if year == 2019 else \"accident.csv\"\n",
    "    file_path = f\"raw/FARS{year}NationalCSV/{filename}\"\n",
    "    data = pd.read_csv(file_path, encoding=\"latin1\", low_memory=False)\n",
    "    data.columns = data.columns.str.replace(\"ï»¿\", \"\", regex=False)\n",
    "    data[\"YEAR\"] = year\n",
    "    annual_crashes.append(data)\n",
    "\n",
    "crashes = pd.concat(annual_crashes, ignore_index=True)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(crashes[\"YEAR\"].value_counts().sort_index())\n",
    "print(\"Total crashes\", len(crashes))\n",
    "\n",
    "crashes.to_csv(\n",
    "    \"processed/combined_accident_2019_2024.csv\",\n",
    "    index=False)"
   ]
  },
