  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "9faea735",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "Check for missing values\n",
    "\n",
    "FARS uses number codes for some missing values. We changed those codes in the hour and weather columns so pandas could count them. About 0.75% of crashes had a missing hour, and 5.04% had missing weather. We kept these rows because we could still use the crash date."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 38,
   "id": "7ec31bd3",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "HOUR        1668\n",
      "WEATHER    11234\n",
      "dtype: int64\n",
      "Total crashes 222695\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "missing = float(\"nan\")\n",
    "\n",
    "crash_data[\"HOUR\"] = crash_data[\"HOUR\"].replace(99, missing)\n",
    "crash_data[\"WEATHER\"] = crash_data[\"WEATHER\"].replace([98, 99], missing)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(crash_data[[\"HOUR\", \"WEATHER\"]].isna().sum())\n",
    "print(\"Total crashes\", len(crash_data))"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 39,
   "id": "9fd0db47",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "Percentage of crashes with missing values\n",
      "HOUR       0.75\n",
      "WEATHER    5.04\n",
      "dtype: float64\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "#Calculating the percentage of crashes missing hour or weather\n",
    "total_crashes = len(crash_data)\n",
    "missing_counts = crash_data[[\"HOUR\", \"WEATHER\"]].isna().sum()\n",
    "missing_percentages = missing_counts / total_crashes * 100\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"Percentage of crashes with missing values\")\n",
    "print(missing_percentages.round(2))"
   ]
