  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "beb14e39",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Create the date and find the holidays\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "We combined the year, month, and day into one date. Then we used the holidays package to find New Year’s Day, Memorial Day, Independence Day, Labor Day, Thanksgiving Day, and Christmas Day. We used the actual calendar dates, which gave us 36 holiday dates across six years."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 41,
   "id": "a599455e",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "Holiday dates 36\n",
      "HOLIDAY_DAY\n",
      "0    218657\n",
      "1      4038\n",
      "Name: count, dtype: int64\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "us_holidays = holidays.US(years=range(2019, 2025), observed=False)\n",
    "\n",
    "holiday_names = {\n",
    "    \"New Year's Day\",\n",
    "    \"Memorial Day\",\n",
    "    \"Independence Day\",\n",
    "    \"Labor Day\",\n",
    "    \"Thanksgiving Day\",\n",
    "    \"Christmas Day\"\n",
    "}\n",
    "holiday_dates = [\n",
    "    date for date, name in us_holidays.items()\n",
    "    if name in holiday_names\n",
    "]\n",
    "is_holiday_day = crash_data[\"DATE\"].dt.date.isin(holiday_dates)\n",
    "crash_data[\"HOLIDAY_DAY\"] = is_holiday_day.astype(int)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"Holiday dates\", len(holiday_dates))\n",
    "print(crash_data[\"HOLIDAY_DAY\"].value_counts().sort_index())"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 42,
   "id": "d5ad6f1e",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "holiday_lookup = {\n",
    "    date: name\n",
    "    for date, name in us_holidays.items()\n",
    "    if name in holiday_names\n",
    "}\n",
    "\n",
    "crash_data[\"HOLIDAY_NAME\"] = (\n",
    "    crash_data[\"DATE\"]\n",
    "    .dt.date\n",
    "    .map(holiday_lookup)\n",
    ")"
   ]
  },
  {
