  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "cb684772",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "Choose comparison dates\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "We chose two nearby dates with the same weekday for each holiday. For example, we compared Thanksgiving with the Thursday before and the Thursday after. We used different weeks for Christmas and New Year’s Day to avoid other holidays. The final study table had 4,035 crashes on holiday dates and 6,963 on comparison dates."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 47,
   "id": "61c7c57d",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "Comparison dates 72\n",
      "HOLIDAY_DAY\n",
      "0    6963\n",
      "1    4035\n",
      "Name: count, dtype: int64\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "comparison_dates = []\n",
    "\n",
    "for date in holiday_dates:\n",
    "    holiday_name = us_holidays[date]\n",
    "\n",
    "    if holiday_name == \"New Year's Day\":\n",
    "        shifts = [7, 21]\n",
    "    elif holiday_name == \"Christmas Day\":\n",
    "        shifts = [-14, -7]\n",
    "    else:\n",
    "        shifts = [-7, 7]\n",
    "\n",
    "    for days in shifts:\n",
    "        comparison_dates.append(date + timedelta(days=days))\n",
    "\n",
    "is_holiday = analysis_data[\"HOLIDAY_DAY\"] == 1\n",
    "is_comparison = analysis_data[\"DATE\"].dt.date.isin(comparison_dates)\n",
    "\n",
    "study_data = analysis_data[is_holiday | is_comparison].copy()\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"Comparison dates\", len(comparison_dates))\n",
    "print(study_data[\"HOLIDAY_DAY\"].value_counts().sort_index())"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "b6d46e35",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "Compare the results\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "We calculated the percentage of fatal crashes that involved an impaired driver for each BAC version. Then we averaged the ten percentages. Across all six years, the estimated share was 38.64% on holiday dates and 27.82% on comparison dates."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 48,
   "id": "3b899497",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "Comparison days (%) 27.82\n",
      "Holiday days (%) 38.64\n",
      "Difference (percentage points) 10.82\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "outcome_columns = [f\"IMPAIRED_{number}\" for number in range(1, 11)]\n",
    "\n",
    "rates_by_version = study_data.groupby(\"HOLIDAY_DAY\")[outcome_columns].mean()\n",
    "percent_impaired = rates_by_version.mean(axis=1) * 100\n",
    "\n",
    "comparison_pct = percent_impaired.loc[0]\n",
    "holiday_pct = percent_impaired.loc[1]\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"Comparison days (%)\", round(comparison_pct, 2))\n",
    "print(\"Holiday days (%)\", round(holiday_pct, 2))\n",
    "print(\"Difference (percentage points)\", round(holiday_pct - comparison_pct, 2))"
   ]
  },
